BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BIDA Afternoon Workshop and Evening Contra Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251116T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251116T223000
DTSTAMP:20261030T094249Z
UID:1ca9a8c2-032c-537f-8b98-d08405933a5e
DESCRIPTION:3:30-6:30 Ogres\, Onions\, and Flourishes\; 7:00-7:30 Contra L
 esson\; 7:30-10:30 Contra Dance. Before our regularly scheduled contra dan
 ce\, with Annie Kidwell calling to Good Company (Rohan Wheeden\, Helen Kuh
 ar\, and Cecily Mills)\, Bret Casey will lead a workshop: Join us as we ex
 plore a versatile technique for flourishes from foundational elements to a
  wide array of variations. Instructor Bret Casey brings 16 years of contra
  dance experience and 15 years of partner dance experience together to off
 er a unique perspective on the ways that we can layer improvisational mome
 nts on top of the contra choreography. The workshop will be split into thr
 ee blocks of roughly 50 minutes each\, with two short breaks. Each section
  of the workshop will build on the techniques learned previously\, so we e
 ncourage you to arrive on time. Familiarity with typical contra dance figu
 res will be helpful. Admission will be on a sliding scale from $5 - $20. W
 e will have musical accompaniment by Helen Kuhar on guitar and Rohan Weede
 n on fiddle. This dance is mask-required.
END:VEVENT
